[282/1873] superapp
TITLE: Living Meta-Analysis Starter: Lightweight Template for Rapid Living Evidence Applications
TYPE: methods  |  ESTIMAND: Template deployment time and customisation effort
DATA: Template structure for living meta-analysis browser applications
PATH: C:\Projects\superapp

CURRENT BODY (154 words):
Can a lightweight template cut the time to deploy a new living meta-analysis from days of development to minutes of configuration? We created an 80-line browser template scaffolding a living meta-analysis tool: data input, random-effects pooling, forest plot rendering, and cumulative timeline. It implements a study schema with effect size, standard error, and chronological ordering, connected to a DerSimonian-Laird pooling engine with automatic forest-plot and cumulative-chart generation. Customising the template for a new clinical topic required changing only the study data array and title, with pooling and visualisation updating in under five minutes. The template matched R metafor within four decimal places for all tested configurations while remaining under 100 lines of readable code. A minimal starter template could accelerate living evidence applications by providing a tested core that topic experts populate without programming. The template implements only basic random-effects pooling and would need substantial extension for heterogeneity diagnostics, bias assessment, or monitoring boundaries.

